Node2D wont display where I want it, even when using script to change its GlobalPosition (C#)

I am trying to display a Node2D which contains text and animation when the player enters an interaction zone. The Node2D I am trying to display, called EToInteract, is displaying, but something is messed up with its position and movement. Here is a video of what happening. You can see that the interact display is on the top left, and its not moving. Or rather, it is static on the screen. In my Interaction Manager, I used the following code:
...
Node2D interactDisplay;

public override void _Ready()
{
    ...
    interactDisplay = GetNode<Node2D>("/root/WorldNode/InterfaceManager/EToInteract");
    interactDisplay.Hide();
    ...
}

public override void _Process(double delta)
{
    if (activeAreas.Count > 0 && canIneract)
    {
        ...
        interactDisplay.GlobalPosition = otherBody.GlobalPosition;
        interactDisplay.Show();
    }
    else
        interactDisplay.Hide();
}

otherBody is the purple NPC character you see in the video.
And this is the layout of my World Scene

I am trying to have the interact display to be on top of the NPC constantly, instead of moving around with the player like you see with the video. I though positioning the display's global position to the NPC's global position would work, but that doesn't seam to be the case. Any suggestions?

